From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Verm <183540171+vermingov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:07:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] feat(linux): extension menus, commands, cookies and
 browser data; drops and Krunker

- menus/contextMenus: extensions' items appended to WebKit's page menu,
  under the extension's name when it has several; clicks raise
  menus.onClicked.
- commands: manifest shortcuts matched on a tab's key presses raise
  commands.onCommand.
- cookies: get, getAll, set, remove and getAllCookieStores through
  WebKit's cookie manager, limited to the extension's host access. An
  unspecified sameSite stays Lax: libsoup drops SameSite=None without
  Secure.
- Firefox's contentScripts.register, mapped onto registered scripts.
- history, bookmarks, sessions and topSites, answered by the shell with
  the macOS port's translations.
- Files dropped on a page reach it: wry no longer finishes the drop
  before WebKit sees it. Captures crop in the screen's pixels.
- The discard-safety script no longer wraps addEventListener. Games'
  tamper checks refuse any wrapper and stop loading (krunker.io); a page
  the user typed into now always counts as guarded.
- With the extension trace on, tabs' consoles go to the log.
